Z||000000||fiero56||04-07-2001||06:08 PM||||I've decided I'm taking the wing off of my Formula for good. My problem, is the torsion springs are way too strong without the added weight of the wing.  Is it worth replacing with softer springs, or figuring out a way to attach a few pounds to the underside of the decklid? I need to fix this before I add remote deck release.||||reg||5
Z||000001||btoth||04-07-2001||06:39 PM||||What?  You don't like the catapult deck lid?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||04-07-2001||07:33 PM||||Drew, we just hang a concrete block from the deck when we take the wing off!! (Seriously, I have a set of the wingless deck springs if you want them -- I'll send them if you will email your address............)||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||04-07-2001||07:36 PM||||Hi Terry!<P>How hard is it to swap out the springs? Is it safe? Any particular method to go about it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||04-07-2001||07:51 PM||||it's safe but, I always put a board up against the rear window (don't want it breaking, and hold the deck lid bracket with a come-along while I remove the 13's from the car body..........||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||04-07-2001||07:56 PM||||good idea about the come-a-long. never messed with it, but dont they have several different positions to reduce/add tension instead of changing them ?||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||04-07-2001||09:35 PM||||actually Roger, they do.......they <I>can</I> be adjusted but it is basically a trial-and-error type of adjustment. It's almost as easy to hook a come-along to the rear deck latch loop (on the rear of the trunk) and take the tension off while you take off the mounting bolts and replace it with one that came off of a wingless car.....personally, the "security" torx bolt on the bracket is what drives me nuts.......not very many of those things on a Fiero so you end up buying one bit just for those!!||||reg||1
